course: dictionary
lesson: 7231
title: Physically: body, real or in person
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Physically» is an adverb. It tells you how something is true, and it usually means in a way about the body, about real things, or about being there in person. The clues around it show you which one.
explain: «Being physically active keeps you healthy» is about your body, so physically means in a way about the body. «It is physically impossible to fly without wings» is about what real things can do, so it means it breaks the laws of nature.
explain: To check, ask: what would fit here? Try swapping in a meaning such as "with the body", "in real life" or "in person" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «Physically» means in a way that is about the body, not the mind, as in «physically fit».
fact: «Physically» can also mean in a way about real things you can touch or see, as in «physically impossible».
fact: «Physically present» means there in person, not just on a screen or in a message.
fact: «Physically hurt» means injured in the body.
fact: «Physically challenged» means physically disabled, and it is mostly used in America.
exercise: «Being physically active keeps you healthy.» In this sentence, physically means? | *In a way about the body | In a loud voice | In a hurry | In a way about the mind only
exercise: «It is physically impossible to be in two places at once.» What does physically impossible mean? | Easy to do | Something you must draw | Only sometimes true | *It breaks the laws of nature, so it cannot happen
exercise: Mum says, «I will be physically present at the school play.» What does physically present mean? | *Being there in person | Watching at home on a screen | Feeling very proud | Asleep in bed
test: «I physically can't eat another bite, I'm full.» What does physically suggest here? | Happily | Sadly | *Strongly, your body cannot do it | Quickly
test: Ella asks, «Did you get physically hurt when you fell?» What does physically hurt mean? | *Injured in your body | Sleepy | Lost | Upset in your feelings
exam: «She is physically fit and can run for miles.» Which meaning fits physically here? | Happy in her mind | Loud and noisy | *In a way about the body | In a hurry
